   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "a Cancel arrives BEFORE its Try",
   "originalText": "a Cancel arrives BEFORE its Try",
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "fd_1130",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1156,
   "y": 796,
   "width": 420,
   "height": 45,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100057,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700399,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The subtlest bug: the partition records an OUT-OF-ORDER\nflag, and a later Try checks it and refuses. A tombstone\nfor an operation that has not happened yet.",
   "originalText": "The subtlest bug: the partition records an OUT-OF-ORDER\nflag, and a later Try checks it and refuses. A tombstone\nfor an operation that has not happened yet.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "cn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 862,
   "width": 1011,
   "height": 32,
   "strokeColor": "#b91c1c",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100058,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700406,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Without the out-of-order flag: the Try is delayed, the deadline passes, recovery sends Cancel which arrives first and no-ops,\nthen the delayed Try lands and debits A - and NOTHING will ever compensate it. Money lost. Most TC/C write-ups omit this.",
   "originalText": "Without the out-of-order flag: the Try is delayed, the deadline passes, recovery sends Cancel which arrives first and no-ops,\nthen the delayed Try lands and debits A - and NOTHING will ever compensate it. Money lost. Most TC/C write-ups omit this.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "cn2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 916,
   "width": 1019,
   "height": 65,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100059,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700413,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "What we give up is ATOMICITY: a real millisecond window exists where the system's total is short. Three things make that\nacceptable - the window is one partition round trip; debit-first makes it a deficit nobody can spend; and any global-sum audit\nruns against the EVENT LOG at a committed sequence position, never a live scan of balances, so it never observes the window.\nThat third point is why TC/C and event sourcing belong together here rather than being two independent choices.",
   "originalText": "What we give up is ATOMICITY: a real millisecond window exists where the system's total is short. Three things make that\nacceptable - the window is one partition round trip; debit-first makes it a deficit nobody can spend; and any global-sum audit\nruns against the EVENT LOG at a committed sequence position, never a live scan of balances, so it never observes the window.\nThat third point is why TC/C and event sourcing belong together here rather than being two independent choices.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  }
 ],
